<%# Upstream's example: a bordered box of tags, taller than it is allowed to be.

    The scrollbar is `type: :hover` by default — Radix's default too — so it is
    not there until the pointer is. Radix *unmounts* it; nothing is unmounted
    here, so it ships with `data-state="hidden"` and the controller moves the
    attribute.

    The second one asks for both axes, which is what puts a corner between the
    two bars: each stops short of the other by exactly its thickness, and the
    corner fills what is left. `always` on that one so both are visible in a
    screenshot without a pointer in it. %>
<div class="flex gap-6">
  <%= render(Shadcn::ScrollArea::Component.new(class: "h-64 w-48 rounded-md border")) do %>
    <div class="p-4">
      <h4 class="mb-4 text-sm leading-none font-medium">Tags</h4>
      <% 24.times do |index| %>
        <div class="text-sm">v1.2.0-beta.<%= 24 - index %></div>
        <%= render(Shadcn::Separator::Component.new(class: "my-2")) %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <%= render(Shadcn::ScrollArea::Component.new(
        orientation: :both, type: :always, class: "h-64 w-72 rounded-md border"
      )) do %>
    <div class="w-max p-4">
      <% 20.times do |row| %>
        <div class="flex gap-4 py-1 text-sm whitespace-nowrap">
          <% 6.times do |column| %>
            <span class="w-24">cell <%= row + 1 %>.<%= column + 1 %></span>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
